{"created": "2026-10-23T04:39:32.125922+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-23T04:39:32.434912+00:00", "id": 23585999, "conceptrecid": "23558752", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23585999", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23558752", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23585999", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package: AI Income Rights and the Identification of Declining Work", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23585999", "publication_date": "2026-10-23", "description": "<p>I provide the complete offline replication materials accompanying manuscript v0024 of AI Income Rights and the Identification of Declining Work. This version adds the flagship joint-information figure and its reproducible plotting code and data while retaining the existing scientific results.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The package includes constructed model experiments, interval certificates, numerical checks, figures, and public 2022/2025 Survey of Consumer Finances inputs with replicate-weight descriptive uncertainty calculations. All 39 programs were run and the five raw-input hashes verified before release. Constructed experiments are not empirical calibration; the SCF results do not estimate an AI effect or establish structural validity.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Download all three numbered ZIP files and extract them into the same empty folder. Together they reconstruct the complete 222-file distribution. The separately named complete ZIP in ARTIFACT_HASHES.json is an equivalent local packaging alternative, not an additional required download here. DOWNLOAD_AND_EXTRACT.txt provides the commands. Federal Reserve provenance and rights are retained, and no additional licence grant for author-created material is asserted. SHA256_MANIFEST.json within the scientific archive identifies the exact distribution bytes.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Wright, Craig Steven", "affiliation": "University of Exeter", "orcid": "0000-0001-9374-0507"}], "version": "v0024", "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "typ